Add test for sitemapRoutes. Use an app with override. Need `new PathlandApp` anonymous class or lambda? `PathlandApp` is functional interface; lambda can't override sitemapRoutes. Use anonymous class. Add test:
```
@Test void sitemapRoutesPrefixMounts() {
 PathlandApp docs = new PathlandApp(){ public View newRoot(){...} public List<String> sitemapRoutes(){return List.of("/","/docs","/docs/intro");}};
 PathlandHost host = host(MountedApp.of("/docs", docs), MountedApp.of("/", app("root")));
 assertEquals(List.of("/docs","/docs/docs","/docs/docs/intro"), host.sitemapRoutes());
...
}
```
Wait for mount `/docs`, app route `/` -> `/docs`; `/docs` -> `/docs/docs` (app sees own scope; route `/docs` is a page in the app). That's correct if app declares `/docs`. But for a docs app mounted at `/docs`, pages should have routes `/`, `/getting-started`? In our demo root app, routes are `/docs`. If mounted at `/docs`, they'd be `/docs/docs`. Fine.

Add import `java.util.List` and `View`. Use `ServerFixtures.text`. Let's edit.

